       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, if you're starting therapy or want a lower dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. If so, I'll add a note to the order that it exceeds the usual maximum and was confirmed by you.\n\nIf the patient's blood pressure isn't controlled on 10 mg, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred to going higher on amlodipine."
      }
     ],
